# Patient Naturalist: with two land cards among the three milled (Forest, Island, Memnite) Bot1 chooses one for its hand (Forest); the Island
# is left in the graveyard and no Treasure is made. A second Patient Naturalist on turn 3 mills three nonland cards (Memnites): "If you can't"
# applies - the Island already in the graveyard is not among the milled cards - so Bot1 creates a Treasure token and its hand has no more
# land. The Treasure, a land-less Island fourth from the top, stays: the library keeps the Island untouched.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Patient Naturalist
Patient Naturalist
Memnite
Memnite
Forest
Island
Memnite
Memnite
Memnite
Memnite
Memnite
Island
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Patient Naturalist.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Forest)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Hand = Forest; Memnite; Memnite; Patient Naturalist
? Bot1.Graveyard = Memnite; Island
? Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token = (absent)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Patient Naturalist.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Pass
